+### This build: the gate is off
+
+This tree carries one change: `account::OWNER_GATE` is `false` (`launcher/src/account.rs`). With it
+off:
+
+- Play starts the game without asking the services: the selected account's session when there is
+  one, and the game's own name or the selected offline name otherwise. No account is needed.
+- Offline names can be added and played with no owner signed in (the hidden developer option in
+  `dev_options.rs` is no longer the only way).
+- "Download and prepare" downloads the pinned version from Mojang without an account. A version's
+  files are public at `piston-meta`, `piston-data`, `libraries.minecraft.net` and
+  `resources.download.minecraft.net`; only Horizon's own check was asking for one.
+- The owner screen never opens, and Play is available as if an owner were signed in.
+
+Sign-in still works, and an account that owns the game still gets its session: it is what
+online-mode servers and chat signing ask for. It is just no longer a condition of playing offline.
+Set `OWNER_GATE` to `true` to get the upstream behaviour back.
+
